                <pb facs="0526" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg428"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Powell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-03-05"><hi rendition="#italic">March 5,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 101.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 200, of the 9th ultimo, reporting your visit to the President of the
                    Dominican Republic, during which you conveyed to him the congratulations of the
                    President and Government of the United States.</p>
                <p>Your course is approved, and the Department appreciates the friendly assurances
                    you received from the President.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
